    <string name="guide_link">Android Auto guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title">Prepare Android Auto</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">IVMoto shows Android Auto on your dash. Android Auto needs a one-time setup, and step 4 repeats after you restart the phone or update Android Auto.</string>
    <string name="guide_s1">1. Open Android Auto settings</string>
    <string name="guide_s1d">On your phone: Settings, then search for "Android Auto" and open it. You should see a page that ends with "Version".</string>
    <string name="guide_s2">2. Unlock developer mode</string>
    <string name="guide_s2d">Tap "Version" about 10 times until a message says developer mode is on. A ⋮ menu appears at the top right.</string>
    <string name="guide_s3">3. Allow new cars</string>
    <string name="guide_s3d">Tap ⋮, then Developer settings. Turn on "Add new cars to Android Auto" or "Unknown sources". Go back.</string>
    <string name="guide_s4">4. Start the head unit server</string>
    <string name="guide_s4d">Back on the Android Auto page, tap ⋮ again. The menu now lists Developer settings and Start head unit server. Tap Start head unit server. It is in the same menu, not inside Developer settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_open">Open Android Auto</string>
    <string name="guide_done">I did it, continue</string>
